MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Aenima and Lateralus feel like natural next choices after 10.000 Days because I want more of Tool's heavy sound, intricate rhythms, and extended songs.",
    "American Idiot fits the energetic, melodic guitar music I enjoyed in Chuck; The Young and the Hopeless also appeals for that reason, though it is a lower priority right now."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Kid A, X&Y, and No Strings Attached miss the heavier riffs and intensity I am seeking, even though they are recognizable albums from a nearby period.",
    "Rap, psychedelic rock, and more mainstream rock do not satisfy the same urge as the heavy, intricate music I want now; simply sharing a broad connection to my listening is not enough."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to lean too heavily on familiar albums from around the same era, when the sound matters more to me than when an album came out.",
    "My interest in some melodic guitar records seems to have been stretched into an interest in much softer rock and pop, without preserving the energy that made those records appealing."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent interest in 10.000 Days makes exploring more Tool especially compelling right now.",
    "The repeated heavier records in my history matter: I want forceful guitars and intensity, with room for either intricate playing or energetic melodies."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in energetic guitar music, but missed how strongly my current choices favor heavier sounds and further exploration of Tool."
}
